  "question": {
    "text": "The eccentric angle in the first quadrant of a point on the ellipse $\\frac{x^{2}}{10}+\\frac{y^{2}}{8}=1$ at a distance 3 units from the centre of the ellipse is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "17VSx",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jNp6n",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ZidyU",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ehIKs",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $P(\\sqrt{10} \\cos \\theta, \\sqrt{8} \\sin \\theta)$ be the required point\r\non $\\frac{x^{2}}{10}+\\frac{y^{2}}{8}=1$\r\nWhose distance from centre (0,0) is 3 units. $\\therefore 10 \\cos ^{2} \\theta+8 \\sin ^{2} \\theta=9=9\\left(\\sin ^{2} \\theta+\\cos ^{2} \\theta\\right)$\r\n$$\r\n\\Rightarrow \\quad \\tan ^{2} \\theta=1 \\Rightarrow \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
